  "_comment": [
    "Bundled seed snapshot. Serves three purposes:",
    "  1. Offline/air-gapped operation and CI without network.",
    "  2. Last-good fallback when a live source fails (served with stale=true).",
    "  3. Reproducible fixtures for the test suite.",
    "Every series carries an explicit `provenance` tag which is surfaced in the",
    "dashboard hover cards. `verified` = read from the cited primary source on",
    "the retrieval date. `cached` = primary-source value held from an earlier",
    "read, refreshed verbatim on the first live run. `reconstructed` = derived",
    "from published summary statistics because the underlying series is not",
    "publicly distributed; treated as indicative, never as observation.",
    "`valid_time` is the date the observation REFERS TO, which is not the date it was retrieved. Staleness must be measured from valid_time: an earlier build measured it from the store write, so a seed value written this run reported 0 h age and the stale-data alarm could never fire."
  ],
